# GUIDE.me — what's built, and how to start

Written for: anyone picking this repo up, including future you.

Warivo OS is an open head unit for ordinary electric scooters. An ESP32-C6 on the scooter
measures the things the scooter won't tell you, and a locked-down Android phone displays
them. Built by [enjoys.in](https://enjoys.in), maintainer Mulayam Singh.

This file is the status board and the runbook. [README.md](README.md) is the pitch and the
compatibility matrix; [docs/PROJECT_GUIDE.md](docs/PROJECT_GUIDE.md) is the architecture.

---

## 1. Status at a glance

| Part | State |
| --- | --- |
| **Node firmware** — ESP32-C6, BLE telemetry | Written, never flashed |
| **Warivo Launcher** — 6 panels, kiosk, splash, ride log | Written, **never compiled** |
| Signal-tap audit — throttle, gear, lights | Researched; blocked on multimeter readings |
| Custom ROM (Path B) | **Parked by decision.** Decided + scaffolded in `os/`; needs a phone and a Linux host |
| Boot animation | In-app splash **built**; the real `bootanimation.zip` needs the ROM or root |

Nothing has run on hardware yet. Treat every number in the firmware as a guess until a
multimeter says otherwise.

